-- title:
--   From HTo G Incomplete Part Average Total Eq
-- statement:
--   **The average residual slice mass is the complement of the averaged slice mass.**
--
--   Let $(m,q,d)$ be LDT parameters with field $\mathbb{F}_q$, and let $F$ be a slice-indexed family of polynomial submeasurements. For each $x\in\mathbb{F}_q$, write $R_x$ for the total of `incompletePartSubMeas`, and write $G$ for the total of `family.averagedSubMeas`. The residual total is the identity minus the complete slice total, so
--
--   $$
--   \mathbb E_{x\sim\operatorname{Unif}(\mathbb{F}_q)}[R_x]=I-G.
--   $$
--
--   This identity supplies the incomplete branch in the Bernoulli from-H-to-G bookkeeping and in the final completeness comparison.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToG_incompletePart_average_total_eq`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
